{"type":"text","timestamp":1794052769810,"sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","part":{"id":"prt_1b5e06e1000113C5qF3qeuTBwg","messageID":"msg_1b5e00ef3001722c47g03vLmWe","sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Fix the reviewer-reported performance problem in `TokenBucket.wait_time` at large clock values, add regression tests proving it is fast and correct, then run tests and commit the fix on the current worktree branch.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`.\n- Branch: `crew/1107-8d1f9e`; previous commits: `92fe8b0 init`, `5c88138 Add token bucket rate limiter`.\n- User constraints:\n  - Work unattended inside the worktree only.\n  - Run relevant tests before finishing and report the exact command and actual result.\n  - Commit to the current branch with a clear message.\n  - Never push or switch branches.\n  - If blocked, end with `NEED_HUMAN: <exact question>`.\n- Reviewer requirement:\n  - Root-cause fix for `ledgerkit/limiter.py:55-66`: `wait_time` was far too slow when clock values are large because it stepped `seconds` by one float ulp while reachable clock values near `last_time` are spaced much farther apart.\n  - Use candidate clock-time stepping: start from `last_time + seconds`, then repeatedly `target = math.nextafter(target, math.inf)` until enough tokens would be refilled, returning `target - last_time`.\n  - Add tests with clock starts `1e6` and `1e9`, rates `3`, `7`, and `0.1`, partial balances, fractional `n`, and a few thousand cycles. `wait_time` must return quickly and `try_acquire(n)` must then succeed.\n- Reviewer regression example:\n  - `rate=3`, `capacity=5`, clock at `1000091.6666666677`, tokens `2**-32`, `wait_time(1.5)` was still running after 10 seconds.\n- Current implementation change already applied to `ledgerkit/limiter.py`:\n  - `wait_time` now computes `target = self._last_time + seconds`.\n  - It raises `OverflowError(\"wait_time would overflow\")` if `target` is non-finite.\n  - In a loop:\n    - If `target == self._last_time`, advance `target = math.nextafter(self._last_time, math.inf)`.\n    - Compute `delta = target - self._last_time`, `now = self._last_time + delta`.\n    - Raise if `now` or `elapsed = now - self._last_time` is non-finite.\n    - If `elapsed > 0`, compute `gained = Fraction(elapsed) * self._rate` and return `delta` when `self._tokens + gained >= amount`.\n    - Otherwise step `target = math.nextafter(target, math.inf)` and raise if non-finite.\n  - This verifies the actual rounded `now`, not only `target`, so the returned `delta` should make the next `try_acquire(n)` succeed.\n- Existing tests from the previous commit currently cover:\n  - Full start, failed acquire does not consume, refill over time, cap at capacity, `wait_time` non-consuming, lazy refill, advancing by `wait_time`, many no-drift cycles, fractional rates/capacities, Fraction inputs, backward clock, default clock, thread safety, invalid `rate`/`capacity`/`n`, `n > capacity`, invalid `n` does not mutate.\n- Before the `wait_time` edit, `python3 -m pytest -q` passed with `57 passed in 1.02s`.\n- The `wait_time` edit has not yet been re-tested, new performance tests have not been added, and the fix has not been committed.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Initial `ledgerkit/limiter.py` implementation and `tests/test_limiter.py` were created, tested with 57 passing tests, and committed as `5c88138 Add token bucket rate limiter`.\n- Reviewer identified the slow large-clock `wait_time` correction loop.\n- Replaced the slow ulp-of-`seconds` loop in `ledgerkit/limiter.py` with target-clock stepping using `math.nextafter(target, math.inf)`.\n- Added validation for non-finite `target`, `now`, and `elapsed`, preserving `OverflowError(\"wait_time would overflow\")`.\n- Chose to validate using actual `now - self._last_time` to guarantee the returned wait makes `try_acquire(n)` succeed after float rounding.\n\n### Active\n- Add the reviewer-requested performance/regression tests to `tests/test_limiter.py`.\n- Re-run the full test suite after the `ledgerkit/limiter.py` change.\n- Commit the fix on the current branch.\n\n### Blocked\n- None.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Add tests to `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py`:\n   - Parametrize clock starts `[1e6, 1e9]` and rates `[3, 7, 0.1]`.\n   - Use `capacity=5`, an initial partial `try_acquire(1.25)`, and fractional amounts such as `[0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.25, 1.5]`.\n   - Run about 1000 cycles per parametrization, asserting `bucket.wait_time(n)` returns quickly and `clock.t = float(clock.t) + wait` followed by `bucket.try_acquire(n)` succeeds.\n   - Add a focused regression test for `clock=1000091.6666666677`, `rate=3`, `capacity=5`, tokens `2**-32`, `wait_time(1.5)`, with a time bound and successful `try_acquire(1.5)`.\n2. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`, fix any failures, and record the actual result.\n3. Inspect `git status --short`, stage `ledgerkit/limiter.py` and `tests/test_limiter.py`, and commit with a clear message such as `Fix wait_time large-clock performance`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py`: contains `TokenBucket`; `wait_time` has been modified but not yet tested or committed.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py`: existing test file; needs new large-clock performance and regression tests.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/README.md`: states tests should run with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_money.py`: existing style reference.\n- `/tmp/f.py`: reviewer stress script that was stopped after hitting the slow `wait_time` behavior; not expected to be restarted.","time":{"start":1794052746768,"end":1794052769805}}}
